# Cursor Product Constitution (Permanent)

Read `docs/PRODUCT_CONSTITUTION.md` Part II before any work.

## Purpose

LaunchLens is **not** a project to finish. It is a **continuously growing AI product**.

Cursor does **not** work in Sprint/Epic/Mission/Release/Version/Queue units.

Cursor **improves Production Product forever**.

## Product Loop (no end)

Journey analysis → problem → UX → implement → QA → regression → a11y → responsive → analytics → build → deploy → production check → **Journey analysis**

## Priority (always)

1. Remove blockers · 2. Remove user confusion · 3. Remove wait · 4. AI acts first · 5. No next-action guessing · 6. Success moments · 7. Return visits · 8. Admin visibility · 9. Perf · 10. A11y · 11. SEO · 12. Code quality → **repeat from 1**

## Implement experiences, not features

❌ Decision Card implemented  
✅ User understands **why HOLD in 3 seconds**

## Production only

No Preview-as-goal. All QA on **Production**.

## Ship cycle (no approval)

Implement → QA → regression → build → deploy → production check → commit → push → **continue loop**

## Report only (no questions)

오늘 새 경험 · 개선 UX · 해결 문제 · Known Issues · Production 상태 · 내일 개선 영역

## Forbidden output

완료 · 끝 · 다음 작업 · 승인 · Queue/Mission/Sprint/Epic/Release 완료 · Queue 비음

## Surfaces (always improve)

Landing → Goal → Workflow → Workspace → Decision → Execution → History → Admin · Coach · Evidence · Confidence · Loading · Error · Retry · A11y · Perf · Responsive · Analytics · SEO · i18n · Dark · Code · Architecture · DX

## New features (all three)

Faster · easier to understand · stronger **AI PM** — else **do not add**. Prefer **Journey improvement**.

## Vision

**AI Strategy Project Manager** — `docs/PRODUCT_VISION_V3.md`

## Stop only

Build fail · prod outage · DB/LLM/Billing/Auth cost · security · CPO vision change

## Do NOT use as work goals

Epic · Sprint · Mission · Release · Version · Queue · Area complete · Task complete
